        "id": 1523797
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-20T18:33:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The PD spec has timing requirements for the PDC\u003c-\u003eport partner communication for requesting an RDO, but AFAIK there is no such bound on the PDC\u0027s overhead for processing SET_RDO and reporting back through GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS.\n\nEmpirically, I have observed times in the high-hundreds of milliseconds for the full cycle. I could likely make it shorter than 3 sec, but I don\u0027t see harm in making it generous, esp. since having a mismatch can lead to a poor user experience (e.g. battery trickle charges despite a high-wattage supply being available). Of course if the RDO is activated before 3 seconds, we move on, so this isn\u0027t adding more delay than necessary. Please let me know your thoughts.",
      "parentUuid": "781d6a0b_4b302a40",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 112,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 112,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "3e1d3743134362bbdc7bf2315e9c4369a0927466",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
